<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/M23/current/>
        rdf:type                skos:Collection;
        rdfs:comment            "Governance for vocabularies and list of terms published and maintained by HELCOM (Baltic Marine Environment Protection Commission - Helsinki Commission) and hosted on the NERC Vocabulary Server. HELCOM is the governing body of the Convention on the Protection of the Marine Environment of the Baltic Sea Area, known as the Helsinki Convention. The Contracting Parties are Denmark, Estonia, the European Union, Finland, Germany, Latvia, Lithuania, Poland, Russia and Sweden.";
        dc:alternative          "HELCOM HUB";
        dc:creator              "Baltic Marine Environment Protection Commission";
        dc:date                 "2019-01-22 02:00:04.0";
        dc:description          "The HELCOM Underwater biotope and habitat classification system (HELCOM HUB) provides a framework for defining biotopes in the whole Baltic Sea. Defining biotopes by the same split-rules, enables comparison of the biotopes in different regions of the Baltic Sea (see http://www.helcom.fi/baltic-sea-trends/biodiversity/helcom-hub).";
        dc:publisher            "Natural Environment Research Council";
        dc:title                "HELCOM 'HUB' Underwater Biotope and Habitat Classification System";
        grg:RE_RegisterManager  "British Oceanographic Data Centre";
        grg:RE_RegisterOwner    "Baltic Marine Environment Protection Commission";
        owl:versionInfo         "1";
        skos:altLabel           "HELCOM HUB";
